.TH SIMPLE_SHELL 1 "August 2026" "Simple Shell" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
simple_shell \- a simple UNIX command interpreter

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ./hsh

.SH DESCRIPTION
Simple Shell is a basic UNIX command interpreter written in C.

It reads commands from standard input, parses command arguments,
searches for executable commands using the PATH environment variable,
creates child processes, and executes programs using execve().

The shell supports both interactive and non-interactive modes.

.SH BUILT-IN COMMANDS

.TP
.B exit
Exits the shell.

.TP
.B env
Prints the current environment variables.

.SH INTERACTIVE MODE

Run:

.B ./hsh

Example:

.nf
$ ./hsh
$ ls
$ exit
.fi

.SH NON-INTERACTIVE MODE

Example:

.nf
$ echo "/bin/ls" | ./hsh
.fi

.SH FEATURES

The shell supports:

.IP \(bu 2
Interactive and non-interactive execution
.IP \(bu 2
Commands with arguments
.IP \(bu 2
PATH command lookup
.IP \(bu 2
The exit built-in
.IP \(bu 2
The env built-in
.IP \(bu 2
End-of-file handling
.IP \(bu 2
Basic error handling

.SH COMPILATION

.nf
gcc -Wall -Werror -Wextra -pedantic -std=gnu89 *.c -o hsh
.fi

